{"id":"assistant-6b6903ba-b655-5901-bdf3-b9fe691b1f46","sessionId":"5520421d-98a9-27ac-2202-9d59d8ddce88","turnId":"turn-3f1ac0253484c7573da3c7ab30a80313","inputEntryId":"user-turn-3f1ac0253484c7573da3c7ab30a80313-1","createdAt":1794282611379,"updatedAt":1794282611379,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is complete. Let me provide a summary:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Problem**: Every `save_fact` call was invalidating the entire cached system prompt because it was built as a single concatenated string. Under prefix-based caching, changing any byte (like adding a fact) evicts everything from that byte to the end.\n\n**Solution**: Split `build_system()` in `bot.py` to return two separate text blocks with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`:\n1. First block: Static `INSTRUCTIONS` (byte-identical across users/days)\n2. Second block: Per-user `athlete_context(a, today)` (volatile content with facts, dates, etc.)\n\n**Result**: When `save_fact` adds a fact, only the second block is invalidated. The first block (static instructions) stays cached, reducing the cache miss from ~1000+ tokens to ~240 tokens (the tail).\n\n**Files changed**:\n- `bot.py`: Modified `build_system()` function\n- `ANSWER.md`: Created with explanation of changes and which parts of the colleague's note applied\n\nThe colleague's note was highly relevant — the diagnosis, solution approach, and caching mechanics all applied directly. The tool filtering they mentioned was already implemented in this codebase, so only the system prompt splitting was needed."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
